---

12. Probabilistic forecasting

Instead of:

> "Next month sales = 10,500"



you learn:

> "Expected sales = 10,500
80% prediction interval = 9,600–11,400"



This becomes much more useful for inventory and financial planning.


---

13. Intermittent demand

Very important if you eventually work with inventory/SKU forecasting.

Example:

Month	Sales

Jan	0
Feb	0
Mar	120
Apr	0
May	0
Jun	80


Normal forecasting methods can struggle here.

Learn:

Croston

SBA

TSB

intermittent-demand characteristics



